> D_m^{\mathrm{adapt}}(\Delta T, C) = D_m^{\mathrm{base}}(\Delta T)\,\bigl[1 - B_m(C,\Delta T)\bigr],
> \]
> where $B_m(C,\Delta T)$ is the fraction of baseline vulnerability removed by adaptation. Income-driven adaptation is represented by applying the estimated income elasticity of climate-related mortality to projected changes in per-capita income, yielding an effective vulnerability reduction without explicit spending. For each stylised investment scenario, we obtain a distribution of adapted temperature–mortality trajectories, convert these into monetary damages using the same value of a prevented fatality as in the baseline risk modelling, and express them as annual losses relative to UK GDP.
